/ref 1034 1.0 #edb/ref 17592186045436] [17592186050517 #edb/ref 1035 #uuid "50123c1c-7113-541e-8c4f-047f2eec416d" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050914 #edb/ref 1028 #edb/ref 17592186059719 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050914 #edb/ref 1028 #edb/ref 17592186059720 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050914 #edb/ref 1028 #edb/ref 17592186059721 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050914 #edb/ref 1031 "Calculating the Components of Cartesian Vectors in 2D" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050914 #edb/ref 1033 242 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050914 #edb/ref 1035 #uuid "70d4531e-58aa-5bdc-912a-8ed0ab5a3a22" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186051014 #edb/ref 1027 #edb/ref 17592186048780 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186051014 #edb/ref 1027 #edb/ref 17592186048816 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186051014 #edb/ref 1028 #edb/ref 17592186096650 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186051014 #edb/ref 1028 #edb/ref 17592186096651 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186051014 #edb/ref 1031 "Linear Combinations of Vectors and Their Properties" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186051014 #edb/ref 1033 1105 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186051014 #edb/ref 1035 #uuid "79fb6a4f-4564-5155-81f6-db81bd65e488" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186100672 #edb/ref 1069 "e-4289" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186100672 #edb/ref 1071 "Find the position vector of $A(-1,2)$ in terms of $\\mathbf{i}$ and $\\mathbf{j}$." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186100672 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "1985c614-4597-521c-bb2d-289fab264708" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186100672 #edb/ref 1074 "Our vector is shown in the diagram below.\n\n![](images/26/269326f4375dfad6d05e4468f4831012bde4a57bc85fbdfc7082cc466d3522dd.png)\n\nRemember that in general, if a point $A$ has coordinates $(a_x,a_y)$, then its position vector is given by\n\n$$\n\\overrightarrow{OA} = a_x\\mathbf{i}+a_y\\mathbf{j}\n$$\n\nHere, the point $A$ has coordinates $(-1,2)$, so its position vector is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nOA^(→) &= (-1) \\cdot i + 2 \\cdot j \\\\\n&=-i + 2j\n\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186100674 #edb/ref 1069 "e-4290" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186100674 #edb/ref 1071 "The points $A, B, C$, and $O$ are shown in the picture below. Find the corresponding position vectors, using angle bracket notation.\n\n![](images/92/92eb1531e0e5e308edb85da62149a220166c8bd37fc0f66d600e9a9599731195.png)" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186100674 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "ad6fec65-5309-58e4-b899-3302188f0e91" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186100674 #edb/ref 1074 "For a point with coordinates $(a_x, a_y)$, the position vector is\n\n$$\n\\left< a_x, a_y \\right>\n$$\n\n- The point $A$ has coordinates $(-1,2)$, so the position vector is\n$\\overrightarrow{OA} = \\langle -1,2 \\rangle$.\n- The point $B$ has coordinates $(3, 1.5)$, so the position vector is\n$\\overrightarrow{OB} = \\langle 3, 1.5 \\rangle$.\n- The point $C$ has coordinates $(1,-2)$, so the position vector is\n$\\overrightarrow{OC} = \\langle 1,-2 \\rangle$.\n- The point $O$ has coordinates $(0,0)$, so the position vector is\n$\\overrightarrow{OO} = \\langle 0,0 \\rangle = \\mathbf{0}$." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186100675 #edb/ref 1069 "e-4291" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186100675 #edb/ref 1071 "Let $A(-2,1)$ and $B(2,3)$. Find $\\overrightarrow{AB}$ in terms of $\\mathbf{i}$ and $\\mathbf{j}$." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186100675 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "ed5a0713-9dec-5f91-ae4f-26dcc25ef174" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186100675 #edb/ref 1074 "Our vector is shown in the diagram below.\n\n![](images/76/76c98067c9780e9c903dda8657b67a2db473ecd8ef24e53e2262ba2f46a4293a.png)\n\nWe have\n\n$$\nOA^(→) = a =-2i + j,; OB^(→) = b = 2i + 3j\n$$\n\nNow, from $\\triangle OAB$, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nAB^(→) &= AO^(→) + OB^(→) \\\\\n&=-OA^(→) + OB^(→) \\\\\n&= b - a \\\\\n&= (2i + 3j) - (-2i + j) \\\\\n&= 4i + 2j\n\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186100854 #edb/ref 1037 #edb/ref 17592186050517 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186100854 #edb/ref 1037 #edb/ref 17592186051014 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186100854 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186101253 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186100854 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186101261 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186100854 #edb/ref 1039 "Expressing a Position Vector in Component Form" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186100854 #edb/ref 1041 #edb/ref 17592186100672 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186100854 #edb/ref 1042 #uuid "7fab292c-d43d-50bb-b785-f1e15122c6c7" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186100855 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186101262 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186100855 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186101263 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186100855 #edb/ref 1039 "Expressing a Position Vector in Angle Bracket Notation" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186100855 #edb/ref 1041 #edb/ref 17592186100674 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186100855 #edb/ref 1042 #uuid "63fc6e25-89d7-56fb-bd4c-a4b5637b7711" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186100856 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186101254 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186100856 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186101265 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186100856 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186234391 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186100856 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186234392 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186100856 #edb/ref 1039 "Expressing a Vector in Component Form" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186100856 #edb/ref 1041 #edb/ref 17592186100675 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186100856 #edb/ref 1042 #uuid "49e90ac1-2e90-51de-831b-a061b4ee80ad" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186101032 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186101648 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186101032 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186101649 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186101032 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186101650 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186101032 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186101651 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186101032 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186101653 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186101032 #edb/ref